# Coordinate changes for rank-two binary cubic matrices

These 1,120 untrusted witnesses put each rank-two cubic matrix in the
standard form with the moving plane first. Both inverse identities and the
conjugation identity are verified by the exhaustive checker. This supplies
coordinates for an arbitrary actual four-dimensional supporting space; it
is not an assumed representation classification.

Source application: the cubic-pair argument for Aschbacher--Smith E.6.24,
printed p.255. Generated by `source/generate.py` in this directory.
-/

